0782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"Pauline Hanson's One Nation Party","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Vanessa Bleyer","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11065","person_slug":"vanessa-bleyer","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"}],"name":"Committees — Foreign Affairs, Defence and Trade References Committee; Reference","noes":21,"question":"Maria Kovacic I seek leave to amend general business notice of motion No. 3 standing in the name of Senator Collins. Leave granted. I move the motion as amended: That the following matter be referred to the Foreign Affairs, Defence and Trade References Committee for inquiry and report by 8 March 2027: The use and impact of monetary, expenditure based and numerical restrictions on Department of Veterans' Affairs-funded health treatment, with particular reference to: (b) the use of monetary limits, expenditure thresholds, numerical treatment limits, review points, additional approval requirements, co-contributions or other restrictions affecting access to treatment; (c) the consequences of such restrictions for continuity of care, clinical outcomes and veterans with complex, chronic or multiple service-related conditions; (d) the particular impact on veterans and health service providers in regional, rural and remote Australia; (e) the adequacy of existing statutory protections and options for strengthening legislative protections against monetary and numerical restrictions on veterans' health treatment; (f) the financial, clinical and administrative implications of restricting, removing or legislatively prohibiting monetary and numerical limits on veterans' health treatment; (g) consultation undertaken with veterans, ex-service organisations, health practitioners and other affected stakeholders; and (h) any related matters. Sue Lines The question is that business of the Senate No. 3 standing in the name of Senator Collins as amended be agreed to.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10811","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-09-17/5"}
